{
  "requirement": "The SDK offers these dispatch interfaces. The supplied `ToolAgent` exposes\n`get_node_page`, and `SourceTools` exposes `get_source_page`.\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Graph-tool calls go through the harness's Conversation.\npub trait Conversation: Send {\n    type Output: Send;\n\n    fn dispatch(\n        &mut self,\n        name: &str,\n        arguments: &serde_json::Value,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = std::io::Result<String>> + Send;\n\n    // Other conversation methods omitted.\n}\n\n// Source-tool calls go through the factory's per-conversation ToolSession.\npub trait ToolSession<D: Graph>: Send {\n    fn dispatch<'a>(\n        &'a mut self,\n        name: &'a str,\n        arguments: &'a serde_json::Value,\n    ) -> BoxFuture<'a, std::io::Result<ToolDelivery<D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>>>;\n\n    // Other session methods omitted.\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Every structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.context-tools.pages.fn` is met, and no acknowledgments or gaps apply.\n\n- **`Conversation::dispatch`:** `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent.rs#trait[Conversation]/fn[dispatch]` is declared as `fn dispatch(&mut self, name: &str, arguments: &Value) -> impl Future<Output = io::Result<String>> + Send`. `Value` is `serde_json::Value`, so this matches the requirement. The trait is `pub trait Conversation: Send` with `type Output: Send`, as the requirement states.\n- **`ToolSession::dispatch`:** `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs#trait[ToolSession]/fn[dispatch]` is declared as `fn dispatch<'a>(&'a mut self, name: &'a str, arguments: &'a Value) -> BoxFuture<'a, io::Result<ToolDelivery<D::NodeId, D::EdgeLabel>>>`. The trait is `pub trait ToolSession<D: Graph>: Send`, which also matches.\n- **`ToolAgent` exposes `get_node_page`:** `GraphSession`'s `Conversation::tools` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs` defines the `get_node_page` tool, with a required integer `page` parameter. That `tools` function also extends the list with the extra-tool session's definitions. `GraphSession`'s `Conversation::dispatch` handles `\"get_node_page\"` through `deliver_page`, and routes unknown names to the extra-tool session's `dispatch`.\n- **`SourceTools` exposes `get_source_page`:** `SourceSession`'s `ToolSession<D>::definitions` in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/sources.rs` defines `get_source_page`, again with a required integer `page`. `SourceSession`'s `ToolSession<D>::dispatch` has the signature the trait requires and handles `\"get_source_page\"` by returning the stored page delivery.\n\nI did not open the code that makes `ToolAgent` use `GraphSession` as its conversation. I took that from the `ToolAgent` struct and its `Agent<D>` impl in `tools.rs`, which carry the agent-harness `tool_agent` marking.\n\nThe implementation roots carry `{impl}` references for this requirement, and the supplied roots cover each part of it.",
